 "text": "Hey, nice to hear from you. How are you? It depends on how thick it is. A thin layer like this can usually go right away, while thick ones often need a day or two more drying time. Then I'd lean towards varnishing now and hoping for the best. If it still feels wet, wait longer and try again in a few hours. You can use a thin coat of a quick drying spray as a protection while you decide. Just revenish first if it starts to chip. It' feel firm to the touch, and a sharp edge won't dull the blade. If it still feels sticky, give it plenty more time.",
